### ShelfLife API - Sample Requests (VS Code REST Client format)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1. Health Check
GET http://localhost:5000/health

### 2. Login (Librarian Auth)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "librarian@shelflife.com",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

### 3. Get Books (Public - Filter by Genre & Search)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?page=1&limit=5&genre=Computer%20Science&search=Clean

### 4. Create a New Book (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Refactoring: Improving the Design of Existing Code",
  "author": "Martin Fowler",
  "isbn": "9780134757599",
  "genre": "Computer Science",
  "totalCopies": 3,
  "availableCopies": 3
}

### 5. Register a New Member (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/members
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "name": "Frank Miller",
  "email": "frank.miller@example.com",
  "membershipId": "MEM006"
}

### 6. Borrow a Book (Protected - Atomic operation)
# Replace bookId and memberId with valid ObjectIds from DB
POST {{baseUrl}}/borrow
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "bookId": "650000000000000000000001",
  "memberId": "650000000000000000000002"
}

### 7. Return a Book (Protected)
# Replace borrowId with valid BorrowRecord ObjectId
POST {{baseUrl}}/return/650000000000000000000003
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 8. Get Member History (Protected - computed isOverdue)
# Replace :id with valid Member ObjectId
GET {{baseUrl}}/members/650000000000000000000002/history
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
